guities":[],"behaviors":[{"given":"a citation on the default (YouTube) path with video_url 'not-a-url' (unparseable), video_title 'Test Video Title', snippet 'Relevant text', start_seconds 10, end_seconds 20","id":"AC-1","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"the returned string contains > \"Relevant text\" on its own line — the quoted transcript snippet as an indented blockquote continuation, the same shape the valid paths emit. Red state (repro deferred to red): on the unchanged tree the return is exactly 'Test Video Title (timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' (the issue Background quotes the same string with title 'Test Video'), so a toContain assertion of the blockquote fails and vitest prints that received string, whose tail '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' is the repro record's promised symptom","when":"formatCitation is called with it"},{"given":"the same citation: video_url 'not-a-url', snippet 'Relevant text', start_seconds 10, end_seconds 20","id":"AC-2","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"the returned string starts with '- ' and still contains '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' verbatim — the degraded entry becomes a proper '- ' list item that no longer merges into the previous list item when rendered, while keeping the unavailable-timestamp tail this branch emits today","when":"formatCitation is called with it"},{"given":"a citation with source_type 'dynamous' and an empty lesson_url (''), video_title 'Test Video Title', snippet 'Test snippet text', start_seconds 10, end_seconds 20","id":"AC-3","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"the returned string starts with '- ', contains no '](' (the title stays unlinked — there is no URL to point at), and still contains its > \"Test snippet text\" blockquote on its own continuation line","when":"formatCitation is called with it"},{"given":"a citation whose video_url is 'https://www.youtube.com/' (parses but has no 'v' parameter), video_title 'Test Video Title', snippet 'Test snippet text', start_seconds 10, end_seconds 20","id":"AC-4","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"the returned string starts with '- ', contains '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' verbatim — the same degraded output this branch returns today (exportMarkdown.ts:53) — contains no '[Test Video Title](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=' deep-link, and contains > \"Test snippet text\" on its own line","when":"formatCitation is called with it"},{"given":"a citation with a valid YouTube video_url 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=abc123', video_title 'Test Video Title', snippet 'Test snippet text', start_seconds 10, end_seconds 20","id":"AC-5","kind":"guard","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"the returned string is unchanged from today's shape (kept behaviour): it starts with '- [Test Video Title](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=abc123&t=10s) — 0:10–0:20' and the '  > \"Test snippet text\"' blockquote follows on the next line","when":"formatCitation renders it"},{"given":"a citation with source_type 'dynamous' and lesson_url 'https://community.dynamous.ai/c/module-1/lessons/123' (video_title 'Test Video Title', snippet 'Test snippet text', start_seconds 10, end_seconds 20)","id":"AC-6","kind":"guard","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"the returned string is unchanged from today's shape (kept behaviour): '- [Test Video Title](https://community.dynamous.ai/c/module-1/lessons/123) — 0:10–0:20' with the '  > \"Test snippet text\"' blockquote on the next line, and no 'youtube.com' and no '(timestamp link unavailable)' anywhere in it","when":"formatCitation renders it"},{"given":"a citation with video_url 'not-a-url', with console.warn spied (the invalid-URL fallback path)","id":"AC-7","kind":"guard","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"console.warn is called with '[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \"not-a-url\"' exactly as an existing test asserts verbatim (kept behaviour); the parallel no-v-param warn (exportMarkdown.ts:50–52) keeps its current message too","when":"formatCitation is called with it"},{"given":"a citation whose snippet is '' or whitespace-only, regardless of source_type or whether video_url parses","id":"AC-8","kind":"guard","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation","then":"the returned string is '' (kept behaviour): the early guard at exportMarkdown.ts:22 fires before every branch, so the fixed fallback returns never render a marker-only line or an empty blockquote","when":"formatCitation is called with it"}],"dependencies":[],"invariants":["Only app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts changes in production code; test changes are confined to app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts, where the acceptance cases are added and no existing case is deleted or weakened.","The '- ' list marker keeps originating inside formatCitation (as the valid paths at exportMarkdown.ts:35 and :58 already emit it); formatSources keeps its '**Sources:**' header and newline join unchanged, so valid entries are not double-marked.","The fixed fallback returns keep the valid paths' line structure: one '- ' item line, then the snippet blockquote as an indented continuation ('\\n  > \"snippet\"' with the two-space indent), so multi-citation exports remain one coherent markdown list.","Both console.warn diagnostics keep firing with their exact current messages ('[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \"...\"') on both degraded YouTube branches; the invalid-URL message is asserted verbatim by an existing test (exportMarkdown.test.ts:223–225).","Exact glyphs and formats are preserved: em-dash '—' (U+2014) as the separator before the range, en-dash '–' (U+2013) inside the 'M:SS–M:SS' range produced by the unchanged formatTimestamp.","The empty-snippet early return (exportMarkdown.ts:22) stays ahead of every branch, so the fixed fallbacks always interpolate a non-empty snippet."],"issue":{"number":49,"title":"fix(export): markdown export drops the transcript snippet when a citation URL cannot be parsed"},"out_of_scope":["Backend, schema, and dependency changes of any kind — no new or version-changed packages (vitest and file-saver are already in place).","CitationModal.tsx, Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, and Sidebar.tsx — on-screen citation rendering is untouched; only the markdown export changes.","The valid-URL YouTube path (exportMarkdown.ts:56–58) and the valid-lesson_url Dynamous path (:34–35) — pinned by guards AC-5/AC-6, not modified.","formatTimestamp, the export header, and the filename slug in exportConversationAsMarkdown.","The empty-snippet guard (exportMarkdown.ts:22) and formatSources' joining/header logic.","The console.warn behaviour itself — warnings keep firing on both degraded YouTube paths and are neither removed nor reworded."],"risks":["Repro is deferred to red: the existing suite is green on the unchanged tree per static trace (the kernel's first acceptance run confirms or falsifies this). The promised symptom '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' is demonstrated by a NEW toContain assertion (the AC-1 snippet blockquote), whose vitest failure output prints today's return; a bare startsWith('- ') boolean assertion would print no received string, so the snippet assertion must be the red carrier.","Unicode trap: the symptom and existing assertions need the exact U+2014 em-dash and U+2013 en-dash; an ASCII hyphen typed into a new test would silently assert the wrong characters.","The existing invalid-URL case's name ('should fall back to title-only with unavailable text when URL is invalid') becomes stale after the fix; its assertions still pass, so the case may be renamed but its assertions must not be weakened to force green.","The Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback has no URL to link, so the fix may only prepend '- ' — fabricating any link target would violate AC-3's 'contains no ](' constraint.","New acceptance tests should spy/silence console.warn the way the current fallback tests do, since the fixed fallbacks still warn (noise only, not a failure)."],"summary":"Make formatCitation's three degraded fallback returns in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts match the list-item shape its valid paths already emit: prepend the '- ' markdown list marker and append the quoted transcript snippet as an indented blockquote continuation line — for the Dynamous empty-lesson_url return (exportMarkdown.ts:32) and both YouTube fallback returns (unparseable video_url :46, missing v parameter :53). Exported markdown then keeps every cited chunk's snippet (MISSION.md 'RAG responses with rich citations') and no longer merges into the previous list item. Production change is exportMarkdown.ts only; acceptance cases are added to the existing exportMarkdown.test.ts with every current case still passing.","version":"2.0"},"sha256":"2c71ef4d9ad8558f2b8922bcfcc7f19d779ccf393b8e2e29be894a8f22a22e9c","source":"task-contract.json"},"design":{"content":{"ac_mapping":{"AC-1":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-2":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-3":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-4":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-5":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-6":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-7":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-8":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"]},"allowed_new_files":[],"context_sha256":"95a429ad83b9ce778171fcde885fb999ace4ad3aa87e72d3e915f4d177be6a2f","contract_sha256":"2c71ef4d9ad8558f2b8922bcfcc7f19d779ccf393b8e2e29be894a8f22a22e9c","data_flows":["Citation (empty/whitespace snippet) -> formatCitation -> '' (early return, exportMarkdown.ts:22)","Cit